#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/controls/interface.md:1
#: internal/help/content/controls/interface.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moving Through the Menus"
msgstr "Перемещение по меню"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/interface.md:12
msgid ""
"Press one key to choose. You do not press Enter to pick a menu item. Each "
"item shows its key in brackets, like `(1)`. Press that key and it runs at "
"once."
msgstr ""
"Нажмите одну клавишу для выбора. Не нужно нажимать Enter, чтобы выбрать "
"пункт меню. У каждого пункта клавиша показана в скобках, например `(1)`. "
"Нажмите эту клавишу — и он сразу выполнится."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/interface.md:16
msgid ""
"\"Quit\" (the `0` key) leaves a turn menu (Spending, Attack, Covert, "
"Trading) and moves you to the next step of your turn. You cannot go back to "
"that menu until your next turn."
msgstr ""
"«Quit» (клавиша `0`) выходит из меню хода (Расходы, Атака, Разведка, "
"Торговля) и переводит вас к следующему шагу хода. Вернуться в это меню можно "
"только на следующем ходу."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/interface.md:19
msgid ""
"\"Return\" (the `0` key) leaves a side menu (like the Bank or the System "
"Menu) and takes you back to where you were."
msgstr ""
"«Return» (клавиша `0`) выходит из бокового меню (например, Банк или "
"Системное меню) и возвращает вас туда, где вы были."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/interface.md:22
msgid ""
"The System Menu opens with the `*` key from the Spending menu. It holds "
"extra options like Preferences, Set Tax Rate, and Show Instructions."
msgstr ""
"Системное меню открывается клавишей `*` из меню Расходов. В нём собраны "
"дополнительные пункты: Настройки, Задать налог и Показать инструкции."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/interface.md:25
msgid ""
"If you turn on \"Enter exits Buy menu\" in Preferences, pressing Enter at a "
"turn menu chooses Quit for you."
msgstr ""
"Если включить «Enter выходит из меню покупок» в Настройках, нажатие Enter в "
"меню хода выберет за вас «Quit»."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/interface.md:26
msgid "Press `?` at a menu to open this help."
msgstr "Нажмите `?` в любом меню, чтобы открыть эту справку."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/controls/numbers.md:1
#: internal/help/content/controls/numbers.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Entering Numbers"
msgstr "Ввод чисел"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/numbers.md:12
msgid ""
"When the game asks for an amount, it shows two numbers in brackets, like "
"`How many? (0; 40):`."
msgstr ""
"Когда игра просит указать количество, она показывает два числа в скобках, "
"например `How many? (0; 40):`."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/controls/numbers.md:18
msgid "The left number is a suggested value. Press Enter to accept it."
msgstr ""
"Левое число — рекомендуемое значение. Нажмите Enter, чтобы принять его."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/controls/numbers.md:18
msgid ""
"The right number is the most you can pick. Type `>` to fill the box with "
"that maximum. You can still edit it."
msgstr ""
"Правое число — максимум, который можно выбрать. Введите `>`, чтобы заполнить "
"поле этим максимумом. После этого всё ещё можно ввести меньшее число."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/controls/numbers.md:18
msgid ""
"`k` adds three zeros as you type. Press `1` then `k` and you see `1000`."
msgstr ""
"`k` добавляет три нуля при вводе. Нажмите `1`, затем `k` — и вы увидите "
"`1000`."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/controls/numbers.md:18
msgid "`m` adds six zeros. Press `2` then `m` and you see `2000000`."
msgstr ""
"`m` добавляет шесть нулей. Нажмите `2`, затем `m` — и вы увидите `2000000`."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/numbers.md:20
msgid ""
"If you type a number larger than the maximum, the game lowers it to the "
"maximum when you press Enter."
msgstr ""
"Если ввести число больше максимума, игра снизит его до максимума при нажатии "
"Enter."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/controls/turns.md:1
#: internal/help/content/controls/turns.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Turns and Protection"
msgstr "Ходы и защита"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/turns.md:12
msgid ""
"You get a set number of turns each day. When you use them all, come back the "
"next day for more."
msgstr ""
"Каждый день вы получаете определённое число ходов. Когда они закончатся, "
"возвращайтесь на следующий день за новыми."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/controls/turns.md:15
msgid ""
"New players get New Realm Protection: a number of turns during which you "
"cannot attack or be attacked. It only ticks down on turns you actually play, "
"so you are safe while you learn the game."
msgstr ""
"Новые игроки получают Защиту нового королевства: несколько ходов, в течение "
"которых вы не можете ни атаковать, ни быть атакованными. Это даёт время "
"развиться."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:1
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Treaties and Alliances"
msgstr "Договоры и союзы"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:12
msgid ""
"You can send agreements to other rulers. A treaty starts when the other side "
"accepts it. These are the main agreements."
msgstr ""
"Вы можете предлагать соглашения другим правителям. Договор вступает в силу, "
"когда другая сторона его принимает. Вот их виды."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tariff Trade Agreement"
msgstr "Тарифное торговое соглашение"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:17
msgid ""
"Trade between two realms, with a tax on goods that cross the border. Both "
"sides earn extra income based on population. This is good if you have many "
"people."
msgstr ""
"Торговля между двумя государствами с пошлиной на товары, пересекающие "
"границу. Обе стороны получают дополнительный доход в зависимости от объёма "
"торговли."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Protective Trade"
msgstr "Защищённая торговля"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:22
msgid ""
"Guards along the trade routes. This stops enemies from bombing your trade "
"deals, and makes trade deals cheaper to send and to keep."
msgstr ""
"Охрана вдоль торговых путей. Это мешает врагам бомбить ваши сделки и делает "
"торговлю безопаснее."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "Free Trade Agreement"
msgstr "Соглашение о свободной торговле"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:28
msgid ""
"People and goods move freely, with no border tax. You earn a lot from income "
"taxes. But people mixing across borders can spread low morale and low "
"support, so watch it."
msgstr ""
"Люди и товары движутся свободно, без пошлин. Вы много зарабатываете на "
"налогах. Но смешение народов может ухудшить настроение в других государствах."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Terrorist Prevention"
msgstr "Противодействие терроризму"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:33
msgid ""
"The two realms' intelligence agencies help each other find and stop covert "
"and terrorist attacks."
msgstr ""
"Разведки обоих государств помогают друг другу находить и предотвращать "
"тайные и террористические атаки."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "Intelligence Alliance"
msgstr "Разведывательный союз"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:38
msgid ""
"The two realms give each other covert help in operations, both at home and "
"between planets."
msgstr ""
"Оба государства оказывают друг другу тайную помощь в операциях — и дома, и "
"между планетами."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Technology Agreement"
msgstr "Технологическое соглашение"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:42
msgid ""
"The two realms share science. Each side gains some of the other's technology."
msgstr ""
"Оба государства делятся наукой. Каждая сторона получает часть технологий "
"другой."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full Defense Alliance"
msgstr "Полный оборонительный союз"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:47
msgid ""
"The strongest alliance. You commit a large part of your forces to defend an "
"ally in need. This works only in local (single-board) games."
msgstr ""
"Сильнейший союз. Вы выделяете значительную часть войск на защиту союзника в "
"беде. Это работает в обе стороны."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "Declaration of War"
msgstr "Объявление войны"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:52
msgid ""
"Ends an agreement without causing trouble at home. The treaty is not truly "
"broken until the other realm is told."
msgstr ""
"Прекращает соглашение, не вызывая волнений дома. Договор по-настоящему "
"разорван лишь после ответа другого государства."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "View Treaties"
msgstr "Просмотр договоров"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/diplomacy/treaties.md:55
msgid "Shows your relations with the other rulers in the game."
msgstr "Показывает ваши отношения с другими правителями в игре."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/economy/banking.md:1
#: internal/help/content/economy/banking.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Banking"
msgstr "Банк"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/banking.md:12
msgid ""
"The bank keeps your gold safe and earns interest. Gold in the bank cannot be "
"taken by pirates or raids."
msgstr ""
"Банк хранит ваше золото в безопасности и приносит проценты. Золото в банке "
"не могут отнять пираты или налётчики."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/economy/banking.md:18
msgid "Deposit — move gold from your treasury into the bank."
msgstr "Внести — перевести золото из казны в банк."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/economy/banking.md:18
msgid "Withdraw — move gold from the bank back to your treasury."
msgstr "Снять — вернуть золото из банка в казну."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/economy/banking.md:18
msgid ""
"Take Loan — borrow gold, up to a limit based on how much land you own. A "
"loan grows over time until you repay it, so pay it back before it becomes a "
"burden."
msgstr ""
"Взять заём — занять золото до предела, зависящего от размера ваших земель. "
"Заём растёт со временем, пока вы его не погасите."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/economy/banking.md:18
msgid "Repay Loan — pay back what you borrowed."
msgstr "Погасить заём — вернуть занятое."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/economy/banking.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Investments"
msgstr "Инвестиции"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/banking.md:23
msgid ""
"You can lock gold away as an investment for a number of days. It pays back "
"your gold plus interest when it matures. The interest rate floats — it rises "
"and falls with how much everyone is investing — so check the rate before you "
"commit."
msgstr ""
"Можно вложить золото на несколько дней. По окончании срока оно возвращается "
"вместе с процентами."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/economy/food.md:1
#: internal/help/content/economy/food.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Food Market and Spoilage"
msgstr "Рынок еды и порча"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/food.md:12
msgid ""
"Your people and army eat food every turn. Agricultural regions grow food, "
"and you can buy more at the Food Market."
msgstr ""
"Ваш народ и армия каждый ход едят еду. Сельские регионы выращивают её, а ещё "
"можно докупить на рынке."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/food.md:15
msgid ""
"The market sells food to you for more than it pays to buy it back. So it is "
"not a place to store extra food for profit."
msgstr ""
"Рынок продаёт еду дороже, чем платит при обратной покупке. Поэтому хранить "
"излишки там невыгодно."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/food.md:17
msgid ""
"Food you hold beyond about two turns' worth of eating spoils each turn. A "
"high technology level slows spoilage. Use or sell surplus food rather than "
"hoard it."
msgstr ""
"Еда сверх примерно двухходового запаса каждый ход портится. Высокий уровень "
"технологий замедляет порчу."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/economy/industry.md:1
#: internal/help/content/economy/industry.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Industry"
msgstr "Промышленность"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/industry.md:12
msgid ""
"Each Industrial region makes gold and production points every turn. The "
"points are built into units."
msgstr ""
"Каждый промышленный регион каждый ход даёт золото и очки производства. Очки "
"превращаются в юниты."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/industry.md:15
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Use Set Industries to split your production across unit types by "
#| "percentage. Or use Specialize to send all of your production into one "
#| "unit type. Specializing cannot be undone, so choose with care."
msgid ""
"Use Set Industries to split your production across unit types by percentage. "
"You can change the split at any time."
msgstr ""
"В «Задать производство» распределите выпуск по типам юнитов в процентах. "
"Либо через «Специализацию» выберите один тип для большего выпуска — но потом "
"ничего другого строить нельзя."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/industry.md:20
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Use Set Industries to split your production across unit types by "
#| "percentage. Or use Specialize to send all of your production into one "
#| "unit type. Specializing cannot be undone, so choose with care."
msgid ""
"Specialize marks one unit type as your focus. It does not replace your "
"percentage split. Your industries make more of the specialized unit and "
"fewer of every other unit. Specializing cannot be undone, so choose with "
"care.  Trading with other specialized empires is the most efficient way to "
"get the units you no longer make well."
msgstr ""
"В «Задать производство» распределите выпуск по типам юнитов в процентах. "
"Либо через «Специализацию» выберите один тип для большего выпуска — но потом "
"ничего другого строить нельзя."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/economy/net-worth.md:1
#: internal/help/content/economy/net-worth.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Net Worth"
msgstr "Состояние"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/net-worth.md:11
msgid "Net Worth is your overall score. It ranks every empire (see Scores)."
msgstr "Состояние"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/net-worth.md:14
msgid ""
"It counts mostly your land and your military strength, minus your debt. "
"Gold, food, and people are not counted directly. So a rich empire with "
"little land or army still scores low. To climb the ranks, hold land and a "
"strong army."
msgstr ""
"Оно учитывает в основном земли и военную силу за вычетом долга. Золото, еда "
"и население не считаются по номиналу."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:1
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regions"
msgstr "Регионы"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:12
msgid ""
"Land is made of regions. You buy regions from a market, and the price rises "
"as you buy more. There are eight region types, each with a different job."
msgstr ""
"Земля состоит из регионов. Их покупают на рынке, и цена растёт с каждой "
"покупкой. Есть несколько видов."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coastal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:17
msgid ""
"Best for tourism income. In good times it makes the most gold. But with low "
"public support, your people lose interest and tourism drops sharply."
msgstr ""
"Лучше всего для дохода от туризма. В хорошие времена даёт больше всего "
"золота. Но при низкой поддержке народа туризм рушится."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mountain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:22
msgid ""
"Mines natural resources. Income is lower on average, but steady — few things "
"change it. Mountains also boost how much your Industrial regions produce."
msgstr ""
"Добывает природные ресурсы. Доход в среднем ниже, но стабилен — почти ничто "
"на него не влияет. Горы также повышают выпуск промышленности."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "Desert"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:27
msgid ""
"Good for solar power. Income swings with conditions, but on average it beats "
"mountains and trails good Coastal land."
msgstr ""
"Хорош для солнечной энергии. Доход колеблется, но в среднем выше гор и ниже "
"побережья."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "River"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:31
msgid "Provides a steady river income."
msgstr "Даёт стабильный речной доход."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "Agricultural"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:35
msgid "Grows food. This is your main source of food if you are not buying it."
msgstr "Выращивает еду. Это главный источник еды, если вы её не покупаете."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "Urban"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:40
msgid ""
"Home to your people. More urban regions means more people can live in your "
"empire."
msgstr ""
"Дом вашего народа. Чем больше городских регионов, тем больше людей может "
"жить в империи."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "Industrial"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:45
msgid ""
"Builds military each turn. In some games this is your only way to get new "
"units.  A good base of Mountain regions makes your industry produce more."
msgstr ""
"Строит военных каждый ход. В некоторых играх это единственный способ "
"получить новые юниты. Хорошая база из гор повышает выпуск."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "Technology"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/regions.md:50
msgid ""
"Raises your efficiency. A larger share of Technology regions boosts your "
"income and your army and lowers some upkeep. Bigger empires need more "
"Technology to get the same benefit."
msgstr ""
"Повышает эффективность. Большая доля технологических регионов увеличивает "
"доход и армию и снижает содержание."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/economy/taxes.md:1
#: internal/help/content/economy/taxes.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Taxes, Support, and Riots"
msgstr "Налоги, поддержка и бунты"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/taxes.md:12
msgid ""
"Your tax rate sets how much gold you collect from your people, and it shapes "
"their mood."
msgstr ""
"Налоговая ставка определяет, сколько золота вы собираете с народа, и влияет "
"на его настроение."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/taxes.md:16
msgid ""
"Popular Support drifts each turn toward a target set by your tax rate. A "
"steady, moderate tax rate keeps Support near its highest. High taxes push "
"Support down.  Low Support badly cuts your Coastal (tourism) income."
msgstr ""
"Поддержка народа каждый ход стремится к цели, заданной налоговой ставкой. "
"Умеренная стабильная ставка держит её высокой."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/taxes.md:18
msgid ""
"Riots grow more likely as your tax rate climbs past a safe level. A riot "
"crashes your Support and drives off part of your population. Raise taxes "
"with care."
msgstr ""
"Бунты становятся вероятнее по мере роста налога выше безопасного уровня. "
"Бунт обрушивает поддержку и прогоняет часть народа."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/economy/trading.md:1
#: internal/help/content/economy/trading.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trading"
msgstr "Торговля"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/economy/trading.md:12
msgid ""
"From the Trading menu you can send gold directly to another empire as a "
"trade deal, with no strings attached. Use it to help an ally, or to move "
"gold to a friend on your board."
msgstr ""
"Из меню торговли можно напрямую отправить золото другой империи как торговый "
"подарок, без условий."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/interbbs/leagues.md:1
#: internal/help/content/interbbs/leagues.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Leagues and Inter-BBS Play"
msgstr "Лиги и межсистемная (Inter-BBS) игра"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/interbbs/leagues.md:13
msgid ""
"Some games link many boards together into one world. Your goal grows from "
"beating the local rulers to helping your board beat other boards. Teamwork "
"matters."
msgstr ""
"Некоторые игры связывают множество досок в один мир. Ваша цель вырастает от "
"победы над местными правителями до победы над другими планетами."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/interbbs/leagues.md:17
msgid ""
"Group Attack — several rulers on your board join one strike against a "
"distant enemy. The gains are shared among those who take part."
msgstr ""
"Групповая атака — несколько правителей вашей доски объединяются в один удар "
"по дальнему врагу. Добыча делится по вкладу."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/interbbs/leagues.md:17
msgid "IP Scores — see how the boards rank against each other."
msgstr "Межпланетный счёт — посмотреть, как доски соотносятся друг с другом."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/interbbs/leagues.md:20
msgid ""
"A league game has a set length. When it ends, the world resets and a new "
"game begins."
msgstr ""
"У лиговой игры есть заданная длительность. По её окончании мир сбрасывается "
"и начинается новая игра."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/interbbs/leagues.md:21
msgid ""
"These features appear only when the game is set up for inter-BBS or league "
"play."
msgstr ""
"Эти возможности появляются только когда игра настроена на межсистемную или "
"лиговую игру."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/military/headquarters.md:1
#: internal/help/content/military/headquarters.md:8
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "HeadQuarters"
msgstr "Штаб"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/headquarters.md:12
msgid ""
"Your HeadQuarters coordinates your army. It is a one-time building project "
"that advances a little each turn until it is complete."
msgstr ""
"Ваш штаб управляет армией. Это единовременный строительный проект, который "
"каждый ход понемногу продвигается, пока не будет завершён."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/headquarters.md:15
msgid ""
"While it is being built — and more so once finished — it raises how much "
"your Tanks add to both attack and defense. Enemies can bomb your HQ with "
"covert operations to weaken your tanks."
msgstr ""
"Пока штаб строится — и ещё сильнее по завершении — он увеличивает вклад "
"ваших танков в атаку и защиту."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:1
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Units"
msgstr "Юниты"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:11
msgid "Your army is built from these units. Each one has a job."
msgstr "Ваша армия состоит из этих юнитов. У каждого своя задача."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troopers"
msgstr "Пехота"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:17
msgid ""
"Troopers fight on both attack and defense, but they are weak at each. They "
"are cheap to buy and cheap to keep. They eat more food than other units. "
"They help you defend against Sabre missile attacks."
msgstr "Пехота"

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Jets"
msgstr "Истребители"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:24
msgid ""
"Jets attack only. They cannot defend. One jet is about twice as strong on "
"attack as a trooper. Jets are cheap to buy but cost a lot to keep. They need "
"carriers to reach a battle: one carrier moves 100 jets. An enemy SDI shield "
"cuts your jets' strength by about a quarter."
msgstr "Истребители"

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "Turrets"
msgstr "Турели"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:30
msgid ""
"Turrets defend only. One turret is about twice as strong on defense as a "
"trooper. They shoot down attacking jets, destroy tanks, and kill troops. "
"They also help stop incoming missiles. Covert operations cannot destroy them."
msgstr "Турели"

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tanks"
msgstr "Танки"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:36
msgid ""
"Tanks are the best all-around unit. They are strong on both attack and "
"defense.  They cost a lot to buy but little to keep. A strong HeadQuarters "
"and good morale make your tanks even stronger. Tanks help you defend against "
"chemical attacks."
msgstr "Танки"

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bombers"
msgstr "Бомбардировщики"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:42
msgid ""
"Bombers have no attack or defense strength of their own. They carry "
"payloads.  Missiles and interplanetary bombings need bombers to deliver "
"them. In a regular attack, your bombers destroy the enemy jets that are "
"sitting on the ground."
msgstr "Бомбардировщики"

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "Carriers"
msgstr "Авианосцы"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:47
msgid ""
"Carriers move your jets to a battle and carry goods for trade. One carrier "
"moves up to 100 jets."
msgstr "Авианосцы"

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "Covert Agents"
msgstr "Тайные агенты"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:52
msgid ""
"Agents run covert operations, such as spying and sabotage. Having many "
"agents also helps defend you against enemy covert operations."
msgstr ""
"Агенты проводят тайные операции — шпионаж и диверсии. Множество агентов "
"также помогает защищаться от вражеских тайных операций."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/military/units.md:56
msgid ""
"A HeadQuarters coordinates your army. A strong HQ makes your tanks much more "
"effective. Enemies can bomb your HQ to weaken your tanks."
msgstr ""
"Штаб управляет армией. Сильный штаб делает ваши танки гораздо эффективнее. "
"Враги могут бомбить ваш штаб, чтобы ослабить его."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:1
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attacks"
msgstr "Атаки"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:11
msgid "You can strike other empires in several ways."
msgstr "Атаковать другие империи можно несколькими способами."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regular Attack"
msgstr "Обычная атака"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:17
msgid ""
"A direct assault with your army. Your attack strength is compared to the "
"enemy's defense. If you win, you capture some of their regions and take some "
"gold. Your bombers first destroy the enemy jets that are on the ground."
msgstr ""
"Прямой удар вашей армией. Ваша сила атаки сравнивается с защитой врага. При "
"победе вы отнимаете у него землю."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nuclear Attack"
msgstr "Ядерная атака"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:23
msgid ""
"Turns some of the enemy's regions into waste. It costs a lot, and the cost "
"grows with the size of the target. Large numbers of enemy turrets can shoot "
"down some of the missiles."
msgstr ""
"Превращает часть регионов врага в пустошь. Стоит дорого, и цена растёт с "
"размером цели."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chemical Attack"
msgstr "Химическая атака"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:28
msgid ""
"Kills many of the enemy's people and troopers, but harms fewer regions. "
"Enemy tanks help defend against it."
msgstr ""
"Убивает много людей и пехоты врага, но вредит меньшему числу регионов. Танки "
"врага помогают защищаться от неё."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Biological Attack"
msgstr "Биологическая атака"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:32
msgid "Harms the enemy's people and troopers, but not their land."
msgstr "Наносит вред людям и пехоте врага, но не его земле."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gooie Kablooie"
msgstr "Gooie Kablooie"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:39
msgid ""
"The ultimate weapon, aimed at a whole enemy planet rather than one empire. "
"The whole board funds it, and only one can exist at a time. It takes a few "
"days to build, then strikes every empire on the target planet. Defenders can "
"send jets to shoot it down before it finishes."
msgstr ""
"Абсолютное оружие, нацеленное на целую вражескую планету, а не на одну "
"империю. Его финансирует вся планета, а урон огромен."

#. type: Title ##
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "SDI Program"
msgstr "Программа СОИ"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/attacks.md:44
msgid ""
"A shield you fund. When it is complete, it destroys about half of the "
"missiles fired at you and cuts attacking jets' strength by about a quarter. "
"Technology regions lower its upkeep."
msgstr ""
"Щит, который вы финансируете. По завершении он уничтожает около половины "
"выпущенных по вам ракет и ослабляет вражеские истребители и бомбардировщики."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:1
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Covert Operations"
msgstr "Тайные операции"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:13
msgid ""
"Covert operations are secret missions run by your agents. Success depends on "
"how many agents you have compared to the target. More agents means a better "
"chance.  Keeping many agents also defends you against enemy covert "
"operations."
msgstr ""
"Тайные операции — это секретные миссии ваших агентов. Успех зависит от того, "
"сколько у вас агентов по сравнению с целью. Больше агентов — выше шанс. "
"Множество агентов также защищает вас от вражеских тайных операций."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:15
msgid "Common operations:"
msgstr "Основные операции:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:29
msgid "Send Spy — read the enemy's defensive strength."
msgstr "Послать шпиона — узнать оборонительную силу врага."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:29
msgid ""
"Spy on Relations — reveal all of the enemy's treaties (useful before a war)."
msgstr ""
"Шпионить за отношениями — раскрыть все договоры врага (полезно перед войной)."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:29
msgid ""
"Special Operations — sabotage the enemy army, destroying a share of their "
"troopers."
msgstr "Спецоперации — саботировать армию врага, уничтожив часть его пехоты."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:29
msgid ""
"Bomb Intelligence — kill enemy agents, so your later missions land more "
"easily. Use this one first."
msgstr ""
"Разбомбить разведку — убить агентов врага, чтобы ваши последующие миссии "
"удавались легче. Применяйте её первой."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:29
msgid ""
"Stir Revolts — spread propaganda that lowers the enemy's public support, "
"which weakens their troopers and their economy."
msgstr ""
"Разжечь бунты — распространить пропаганду, снижающую поддержку врага, что "
"ослабляет его пехоту и экономику."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:29
msgid "Bomb Airbases — destroy enemy jets that are on the ground."
msgstr "Разбомбить аэродромы — уничтожить истребители врага на земле."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:29
msgid "Bomb Food Stores — destroy much of the enemy's food reserve."
msgstr ""
"Разбомбить склады еды — уничтожить большую часть продовольственного запаса "
"врага."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:29
msgid ""
"Bomb HQ — weaken the enemy's HeadQuarters, making their tanks less effective."
msgstr ""
"Разбомбить штаб — ослабить штаб врага, из-за чего его танки станут менее "
"эффективны."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:29
msgid ""
"Bribery — buy off an agent inside the enemy, so that their covert operations "
"against you fail from then on."
msgstr ""
"Подкуп — купить агента внутри вражеского государства, чтобы его тайные "
"операции против вас впредь проваливались."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/covert.md:31
msgid ""
"An Intelligence Alliance adds half of an ally's agents to your covert "
"strength.  A Terrorist Prevention treaty adds half an ally's agents to your "
"defense."
msgstr ""
"Разведывательный союз добавляет к вашей тайной силе половину агентов "
"союзника. Договор о противодействии терроризму добавляет к вашей защите "
"половину агентов союзника."

#. type: Title #
#: internal/help/content/warfare/pirates.md:1
#: internal/help/content/warfare/pirates.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pirates"
msgstr "Пираты"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/pirates.md:12
msgid ""
"Nine pirate factions live in the world. Their strength is random. Any "
"faction can be the strongest, so do not assume the last one on the list is "
"the hardest."
msgstr ""
"В мире живут девять пиратских группировок. Их сила случайна. Сильнейшей "
"может быть любая, поэтому проверяйте, прежде чем нападать."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/pirates.md:16
msgid ""
"Pirates raid players at random. When they raid you, they carry off some of "
"your troopers, jets, turrets, tanks, agents, and gold. They never take "
"bombers, carriers, or your regions. A single raid takes at most 24,999 of "
"any one thing."
msgstr "Пираты"

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/pirates.md:19
msgid ""
"When a pirate raids, the game gives it new regions. So a pirate that just "
"raided someone is fatter and holds more land. If no one fights them, pirates "
"grow."
msgstr ""
"Когда пират совершает набег, игра даёт ему новые регионы. Так пират, только "
"что кого-то ограбивший, толще и является лучшей целью."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/pirates.md:24
msgid ""
"You can attack a pirate faction to take goods back. A win gives you back "
"about a fifth of what that faction holds — its stolen units, its gold, and "
"some of its regions. It takes several hits to drain a fat faction. A loss "
"costs you a share of the forces you sent."
msgstr ""
"Можно напасть на пиратскую группировку, чтобы вернуть добро. Победа "
"возвращает вам около пятой части того, чем владеет эта группировка."

#. type: Plain text
#: internal/help/content/warfare/pirates.md:25
msgid "Tip: military parked in the Trading Market is safe from pirate raids."
msgstr ""
"Совет: войска, оставленные на Торговом рынке, защищены от пиратских набегов."

#. type: Title #
#: README.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Immortal Barons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:7
msgid ""
"Immortal Barons is a turn-based strategy game for the terminal. You rule a "
"barony in a ruined, post-apocalyptic world. You buy land, feed your people, "
"build an army, and fight rival empires. The goal is to have the highest net "
"worth when the turns run out, or to conquer everyone else."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:10
msgid ""
"The game is written in Go. It is an independent remake, inspired by the "
"1990s BBS door game *Barren Realms Elite*. See [Heritage](#heritage) below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Early work in progress.** Immortal Barons is not ready for real\n"
"> play-testing or inter-BBS (IBBS) play yet. Mechanics are still changing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: README.md:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "Status"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:20
msgid ""
"In development — not yet released. Immortal Barons is a persistent, multi-"
"user BBS door game: each caller has a lasting empire in one shared world; "
"you play your turns, and other barons (and any AI) act on their own turns. "
"The game runs locally or as a native BBS door."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Works now:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid "Full menu system with single-key commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Persistent shared world: your empire is saved between calls, keyed by your "
"BBS handle; one player at a time (exclusive lock); a daily maintenance step"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Per-turn economy (idle empires stagnate); turns-per-day and new-realm "
"protection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Economy: buy and sell land at a **rising market price**, buy food, recruit "
"troopers, build jets/turrets/tanks/carriers, recruit covert agents"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid "Bank: deposit, withdraw, take a loan, repay, invest (about 1%/turn)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"War: conventional attack (offense vs. defense), plus **nuclear, chemical, "
"and biological** strikes and **pirate raids**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Covert ops (agent-count decides success): spy for intel, sabotage, and "
"strikes on the enemy's intelligence, airbases, food stores, and HeadQuarters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Region types (coastal, mountain, desert, river, agricultural, urban, "
"industrial, technology) and a food market"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Diplomacy: typed treaties (defense, trade, intelligence) with their effects"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid "Sysop configuration editor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Industry: set production percentages per unit, or specialize (permanent)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Messages: player-to-player mail with a multi-line editor, and a planetary "
"bulletin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"A planetary news feed: battles, nuclear/chemical/biological strikes, pirate "
"raids, and tax riots are broadcast to everyone"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid "Write Macros: record a Ctrl-key to replay a sequence of keystrokes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Localization: menus, prompts, and the help database render in the caller's "
"language (English, German, and Russian so far)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid "\"While you were away\" event log for asynchronous play"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:49
msgid "Scores and net worth"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Planned (not built yet):**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:57
msgid "Leagues that reset on a timer and crown a winner"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:57
msgid "The Quick Strike and Extended Battle attack variants"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:57
msgid ""
"Inter-BBS (IBBS) live play (the packet exchange — scores, news, and group "
"attacks — works and is tested; validation under real BBS software is still "
"pending)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: README.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build and run"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:63
msgid ""
"You need Go 1.26 or newer. The game builds and runs anywhere Go does — "
"Linux, macOS, Windows, and the BSDs (DOS is not supported). It plays locally "
"or as a native BBS door."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: README.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"go build -o barons ./cmd/barons\n"
"./barons\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:70
msgid "Or run it directly:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: README.md:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "go run ./cmd/barons\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: README.md:75
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running as a BBS door"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:79
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The game is one program: `barons-door`. It runs as a native door under "
#| "modern BBS software such as Synchronet or Mystic. You do not need DOSBox "
#| "or DOSEMU."
msgid ""
"Immortal Barons can run as a native door under modern BBS software such as "
"Synchronet or Mystic. Build the door front-end:"
msgstr ""
"Игра — это одна программа: `barons-door`. Она работает как нативная дверь "
"под современным ПО BBS, например Synchronet или Mystic. DOSBox или DOSEMU не "
"нужны."

#. type: Fenced code block
#: README.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "go build -o barons-door ./cmd/barons-door\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:86
msgid ""
"The BBS writes a dropfile when a caller starts the door. Configure your BBS "
"to run `barons-door` and pass the dropfile path:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: README.md:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "barons-door -dropfile /path/to/node/DOOR32.SYS\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:95
msgid ""
"It reads `DOOR32.SYS` (preferred) or `DOOR.SYS` to learn the caller's name, "
"node, time left, and whether their terminal supports ANSI. The BBS connects "
"the caller to the door over standard input and output. With no `-dropfile`, "
"it looks for `DOOR32.SYS` or `DOOR.SYS` in the working directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:99
msgid ""
"Callers share one persistent world: each caller's empire is saved between "
"calls, keyed by their BBS handle. A nightly maintenance step (`barons-door "
"-maint`) advances the world."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:103
msgid ""
"Full setup instructions for local and inter-BBS play — registering the door, "
"daily maintenance, the node list, and starting a fresh game with `barons-"
"door -reset` — are in [`docs/sysop-guide.md`](docs/sysop-guide.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: README.md:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running in a browser (experimental)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:107
msgid ""
"A browser front-end serves the game over Server-Sent Events with xterm.js:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: README.md:108
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"go build -o barons-web ./cmd/barons-web\n"
"./barons-web -addr :8080\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:116
msgid ""
"Open `http://localhost:8080`. Each browser gets its own game session. This "
"is early and loads xterm.js from a CDN; the assets should be vendored (or "
"integrity-pinned) before any real deployment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: README.md:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to play"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:122
msgid ""
"The game uses single keypresses. You do not press Enter to choose a menu "
"item. When the game asks for a number (for example, how much land to buy), "
"type the number and press Enter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:124
msgid "From the main menu:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:131
msgid "`B` — Buy or sell land, food, and military units"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:131
msgid "`K` — Visit the bank"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:131
msgid "`W` — Attack a rival empire"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:131
msgid "`D` — Display your empire status and the scores"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:131
msgid "`N` — End your turn (this runs the daily update for the whole world)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:131
msgid "`Q` — Quit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:135
msgid ""
"Each game lasts 20 turns. Build your army before you attack. A rival defends "
"its home land, so a weak attack will lose. Watch your food: if your people "
"run out of food, they starve and your empire shrinks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: README.md:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "Design"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:140
msgid ""
"The design notes are in [`docs/superpowers/specs/`](docs/superpowers/specs/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:145
msgid ""
"The code is split so that the game logic does not know how it is shown to "
"the player. The engine only reads keypresses from, and writes text to, a "
"`Session`. This makes it possible to add a BBS-door front-end and a web "
"front-end later without changing the game rules."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:151
msgid "`cmd/barons` — the local terminal front-end"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:151
msgid "`internal/session` — the input/output abstraction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:151
msgid "`internal/ansi` — terminal color and screen codes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:151
msgid "`internal/menu` — the menu engine and the menu tree"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:151
msgid "`internal/game` — the world, economy, turn engine, and combat"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: README.md:152
#, no-wrap
msgid "Heritage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:161
msgid ""
"Immortal Barons is a tribute to *Barren Realms Elite*, created by Mehul "
"Patel and later maintained by [John Dailey](https://"
"www.johndaileysoftware.com/).  This project shares that game's ideas and "
"feel, but it does not use any of its code, text, or artwork.  Game rules and "
"mechanics are not covered by copyright, so this is a fresh implementation of "
"the concept. It is not affiliated with, or endorsed by, the original authors."
msgstr ""

