#. type: Title #
#: docs/playing.md:1
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Sysop Guide — Running Immortal Barons"
msgid "Playing Immortal Barons"
msgstr "Руководство сисопа — запуск Immortal Barons"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/playing.md:6
msgid ""
"Immortal Barons is a strategy game. You rule an empire in a broken world. "
"You build an economy, raise an army, and compete with other rulers. You play "
"a set number of turns each day."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/playing.md:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "The player guide is the in-game help"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/playing.md:11
msgid ""
"The guide lives inside the game as **categorized help**. Open it from the "
"Game Menu (Help Database), or press `?` at a menu. It is organized by "
"category:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/playing.md:18
msgid "**Controls** — moving through the menus, entering numbers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/playing.md:18
msgid "**Military** — units and their roles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/playing.md:18
msgid "**Economy** — regions, food, banking"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/playing.md:18
msgid "**Warfare** — attacks, covert operations, pirates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/playing.md:18
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Treaties and Alliances"
msgid "**Diplomacy** — treaties and alliances"
msgstr "Договоры и союзы"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/playing.md:18
msgid "**Inter-BBS** — leagues and group attacks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/playing.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same content is the single source for a web guide too. It lives as Markdown\n"
"under `internal/help/content/<category>/`, and is translated with po4a (see\n"
"`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-docs-help-localization-design.md`). Edit the\n"
"topic files there; the in-game help and the web guide both come from them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sysop Guide — Running Immortal Barons"
msgstr "Руководство сисопа — запуск Immortal Barons"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:6
msgid ""
"This guide is for the BBS operator (the sysop). It explains how to set up "
"the game on your board, and how to join an inter-BBS league. Players do not "
"need to read this."
msgstr ""
"Это руководство для оператора BBS (сисопа). Оно объясняет, как настроить "
"игру на вашей доске и присоединиться к межсистемной лиге. Игрокам его читать "
"не нужно."

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "What you need"
msgstr "Что нужно"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:11
msgid ""
"The game is one program: `barons-door`. It runs as a native door under "
"modern BBS software such as Synchronet or Mystic. You do not need DOSBox or "
"DOSEMU."
msgstr ""
"Игра — это одна программа: `barons-door`. Она работает как нативная дверь "
"под современным ПО BBS, например Synchronet или Mystic. DOSBox или DOSEMU не "
"нужны."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:14
msgid ""
"The game keeps all its files in one data directory (default `./data`). Point "
"the `-data` option at it."
msgstr ""
"Игра хранит все файлы в одном каталоге данных (по умолчанию `./data`). "
"Укажите на него параметром `-data`."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:16
msgid "Run `barons-door -help` to see all the command-line options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "First-time setup"
msgstr "Первоначальная настройка"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:20
msgid "Run the setup once to create the config file:"
msgstr "Запустите настройку один раз, чтобы создать файл конфигурации:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "barons-door -setup -data /path/to/data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:31
msgid ""
"This opens the **Configuration Editor**: a menu of every game rule (turns "
"per day, protection turns, land and market settings, interest and investment "
"rates, tax and region limits, costs and attack settings, number of AI "
"barons, game length, and more). Change what you like, then press `0` to save "
"`config.json`, or `Q` to cancel. `-setup` only writes the config; it does "
"not create or change any game world (the world is created when your first "
"caller logs in)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:36
msgid ""
"There is also a **`-reset`** command described later. It opens the *same* "
"Configuration Editor, but after you save it also **starts a fresh game** "
"(clears all empires and re-seeds the AI). Use `-setup` when you first "
"install the game, and `-reset` when you want to reconfigure and start over."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "Registering the door"
msgstr "Регистрация двери"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:40
msgid ""
"Set up the game as an external program (a \"door\") in your BBS software."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:45
msgid ""
"The game reads **DOOR32.SYS** (both Synchronet and Mystic write it) or "
"**DOOR.SYS**. Point the game at it with `-dropfile`, or let it search the "
"current directory."
msgstr ""
"Игра читает **DOOR32.SYS** (его пишут и Synchronet, и Mystic) или "
"**DOOR.SYS**. Укажите на него параметром `-dropfile` или дайте игре найти "
"его в текущем каталоге."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:45
msgid "The caller's handle from the dropfile becomes the name of their realm."
msgstr "Псевдоним абонента из dropfile становится названием его королевства."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:47
msgid "A typical command line:"
msgstr "Типичная командная строка:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "barons-door -dropfile /path/to/DOOR32.SYS -data /path/to/data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "Daily maintenance"
msgstr "Ежедневное обслуживание"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:55
msgid "Run maintenance once a day (a nightly event is the usual place):"
msgstr "Запускайте обслуживание раз в день (обычно это ночное событие):"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "barons-door -maint -data /path/to/data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:62
msgid ""
"This advances the game one day for every day that passed, lets the AI barons "
"take their turns, and refreshes each player's turns."
msgstr ""
"Это продвигает игру на один день за каждый прошедший день, даёт ИИ-баронам "
"сделать ходы и обновляет ходы каждого игрока."

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "Starting a fresh game (reset)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:66
msgid "To reconfigure and start the game over, run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "barons-door -reset -data /path/to/data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:77
msgid ""
"This opens the same **Configuration Editor** as `-setup` (adjust any rules, "
"then `0` to save or `Q` to cancel). After you save, it clears all empires "
"(players re-create their realm the next time they log in) and re-seeds the "
"AI barons on a fresh day one. It does not pick a winner. The old world is "
"saved to `world.json.bak` in the data directory first, so you can restore it "
"if you reset by mistake. Cancelling with `Q` leaves the game untouched."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inter-BBS (league) play"
msgstr "Межсистемная (лиговая) игра"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:82
msgid ""
"A league is a group of boards whose players compete against each other. To "
"join one, turn on inter-BBS play and give your board a name."
msgstr ""
"Лига — это группа досок, игроки которых соревнуются друг с другом. Чтобы "
"вступить, включите межсистемную игру и дайте своей доске имя."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:84
msgid "Edit `config.json` and set:"
msgstr "Отредактируйте `config.json` и задайте:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:90
msgid "`\"IBBS\": true` — turn on the inter-BBS menus."
msgstr "`\"IBBS\": true` — включить межсистемные меню."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:90
msgid "`\"BoardID\"` — a short unique name for your board (your \"planet\")."
msgstr "`\"BoardID\"` — короткое уникальное имя вашей доски (вашей «планеты»)."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:90
msgid ""
"`\"InboundDir\"` — the directory where packets from other boards arrive."
msgstr "`\"InboundDir\"` — каталог, куда приходят пакеты от других досок."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:90
msgid ""
"`\"OutboundDir\"` — the directory where the game writes packets for other "
"boards."
msgstr ""
"`\"OutboundDir\"` — каталог, куда игра записывает пакеты для других досок."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:93
msgid ""
"Ask your League Coordinator for the node list and add it to your data "
"directory as **`ibnodes.dat`** (see the format below)."
msgstr ""
"Попросите у координатора лиги список узлов и положите его в каталог данных "
"как **`ibnodes.dat`** (формат см. ниже)."

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "How packets move (you choose the schedule)"
msgstr "Как перемещаются пакеты (расписание выбираете вы)"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:99
msgid ""
"The game never moves files between boards. It only reads and writes packet "
"files in your inbound and outbound directories. Moving the files between "
"boards is your job, and you choose how often it happens."
msgstr ""
"Игра никогда не перемещает файлы между досками. Она лишь читает и пишет "
"файлы пакетов в ваших входящем и исходящем каталогах. Перемещать файлы между "
"досками — ваша задача, и вы решаете, как часто это делать."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:101
msgid "The inter-BBS step is:"
msgstr "Межсистемный шаг:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "barons-door -planetary -data /path/to/data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:109
msgid ""
"It reads every packet in your inbound directory, applies it, and writes new "
"packets to your outbound directory. It also runs automatically inside `-"
"maint` when inter-BBS play is on."
msgstr ""
"Он читает каждый пакет во входящем каталоге, применяет его и пишет новые "
"пакеты в исходящий каталог. Он также выполняется автоматически внутри `-"
"maint`, когда включена межсистемная игра."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:111
msgid "A common setup:"
msgstr "Типичная схема:"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:118
msgid "A caller plays the game."
msgstr "Абонент играет."

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:118
msgid "After the caller exits, or on a schedule you pick, run `-planetary`."
msgstr ""
"После выхода абонента или по выбранному вами расписанию запустите `-"
"planetary`."

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:118
msgid ""
"Your transport script copies each file from your outbound directory to the "
"inbound directory of every other board (over FidoNet, a sync tool, scp, a "
"shared mount — whatever you use)."
msgstr ""
"Ваш транспортный скрипт копирует каждый файл из исходящего каталога во "
"входящий каталог каждой другой доски (через FidoNet, средство синхронизации, "
"scp, общий диск — что используете)."

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:118
msgid "The next `-planetary` run on each board reads and applies those files."
msgstr ""
"Следующий запуск `-planetary` на каждой доске читает и применяет эти файлы."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:122
msgid ""
"Run it as often as you like. More often means shorter travel times between "
"planets. The in-game \"Travel Times\" screen shows players how recently "
"packets have arrived, so they know how fast operations move."
msgstr ""
"Запускайте его так часто, как хотите. Чаще — короче время в пути между "
"планетами. Экран «Время в пути» в игре показывает игрокам, как недавно "
"приходили пакеты, чтобы они знали скорость операций."

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:123
#, no-wrap
msgid "The node list: `ibnodes.dat`"
msgstr "Список узлов: `ibnodes.dat`"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:128
msgid ""
"The node list names every board in the league. It uses the same simple "
"layout as the original BRE `BRNODES.DAT`. Each board is six lines, and a "
"blank line separates boards:"
msgstr ""
"Список узлов перечисляет каждую доску лиги. Он использует ту же простую "
"разметку, что и оригинальный `BRNODES.DAT` из BRE. Каждая доска — шесть "
"строк, доски разделяет пустая строка:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:129
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1\n"
"Avalon\n"
"363/277\n"
"Orlando\n"
"FL\n"
"USA\n"
"\n"
"2\n"
"Pier 7\n"
"106/477\n"
"Houston\n"
"TX\n"
"USA\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:147
msgid ""
"The six lines are: node number, board (planet) name, network address, city, "
"state or province, and country. Board number 1 is the League Coordinator."
msgstr ""
"Шесть строк: номер узла, имя доски (планеты), сетевой адрес, город, область "
"или провинция и страна. Доска номер 1 — координатор лиги."

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:148
#, no-wrap
msgid "League-wide rules (Coordinator only)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:156
msgid ""
"The League Coordinator sets the rules that must match across the whole "
"league.  These are all the fields marked with a star in the Configuration "
"Editor: turns per day, protection turns, game length, land market and daily "
"land, interest and investment rates, tax and region and player limits, buy-"
"military mode, and the cost, damage, and reward levels. Set them in the "
"Coordinator's own `config.json`, then broadcast them to every board:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "barons-door -league-config -data /path/to/data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:165
msgid ""
"This writes a settings packet to your outbound directory. Each member board "
"adopts the settings on its next `-planetary` run. Member boards accept these "
"settings only from the Coordinator's board (node 1), so no one else can "
"change the league rules. Only the Coordinator's board may send this packet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:166
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Coordinator"
msgstr "Координатор"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:169
msgid ""
"There are two different \"coordinator\" ideas, and they are not the same "
"thing:"
msgstr "Есть два разных понятия «координатор», и это не одно и то же:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:174
msgid ""
"**League Coordinator** — the sysop of board number 1. This person keeps the "
"node list and hands it out to the other boards."
msgstr ""
"**Координатор лиги** — сисоп доски номер 1. Он ведёт список узлов и раздаёт "
"его другим доскам."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sysop-guide.md:174
msgid ""
"**BBS Coordinator** — a *player* your board elects. Players vote in the "
"System menu, and the player with the most votes gets the Coordinator menu.  "
"Votes can change at any time."
msgstr ""
"**Координатор BBS** — *игрок*, которого выбирает ваша доска. Игроки голосуют "
"в системном меню, и игрок с наибольшим числом голосов получает меню "
"координатора. Голос можно менять в любой момент."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Set up the game as an external program (a \"door\") in your BBS software. "
#~ "Your BBS writes a dropfile when a caller runs the door. The game reads it "
#~ "to learn who is playing and how much time they have."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Настройте игру как внешнюю программу («дверь») в ПО вашей BBS. Ваша BBS "
#~ "записывает dropfile, когда абонент запускает дверь. Игра читает его, "
#~ "чтобы узнать, кто играет и сколько у него времени."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "It asks a few questions (turns per day, protection turns, number of AI "
#~ "barons, game length) and writes `config.json`."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Она задаёт несколько вопросов (ходов в день, ходов защиты, число ИИ-"
#~ "баронов, длительность игры) и записывает `config.json`."
